  "description": {
    "text": "Battle Road Autumn 2004 was held in Osaka on 24 October, Tokyo on 7 November and Nagoya on 21 November 2004, in a junior league and a senior and master league. Each player played seven qualifying games, and the top 16 of each league went on to the final tournament. Everyone in the qualifying round got Ryo Ueda's Rocket's Raikou ex stamped in gold with the event's logo, and the top three of each league won the Victory Ring: 18 copies by Pokumon's count.",
